abstract: >-
  A new way to teach higher mathematics. The base is the integers 0-9 read as
  shapes, the premise of the book "The Shape of Understanding": the book's own
  rule, the most symmetric arrangement of n points, realizes every integer
  from 0 to 9 uniquely (the void, point, segment, triangle, tetrahedron, and
  the tetrahedron, octahedron and cube with and without their centres). Each
  base shape is the ground floor of a tower of higher mathematics: the
  simplex, cross-polytope and cube towers (the only regular shapes in every
  dimension), the number tower R-C-H-O, the Clifford tower up to Bott
  periodicity, the symmetry tower (A5 and the unsolvable quintic), the
  lattice tower up to E8, and the harmonic, real-number and growth towers.
  Every forced floor is machine-checked by short numpy scripts; the theorems
  at the tops are cited. An earlier table-based program is archived at the
  tag archive-2026-09-24.
